{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Data Warehouse", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about data warehouse.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Understand information about data and its structure in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.  Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le02ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Look for a data warehouse on the internet. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Study all the information on the website. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "List all the features you can find on there. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a mail to a friend letting him/ her know everything you found on the website.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the mail with a classmate.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I can look for specific information on the internet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can list specific features. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can write a mail describing what I found.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Be Able to and Can", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use  <span class=\"strong\">be able to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">can</span> to talk about actions that you perform according to your abilities.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p> Notice that the only difference between them is that <b><i>be able to </i></b>is more formal than <b><i>can</i></b>.<br /><br />To create a statement using <i><b>be able to</i></b>, follow the next structure.<br /><br /><b>Subject + Verb to be + Able to + Verb + Complement</b><br /><br />Example: <br /><i>I <b>am able to</b> explain everything related to </i>data<i> warehousing.</i><br /><br />To create a statement using <b>can, </b> follow the next structure:<br /><br /><b>Subject + Can + Verb + Complement</b> <br /><br />Example: <br /><i>I <b>can </b>work with data warehouses.</i></p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Modern organizations are able to organize their data in a data warehouse because it works with extent queries, and it helps understanding information at any time in a company.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You need to be able to work with the three different types of data warehouses that exist.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Possessive Forms", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use possessives to indicate that something belongs to the person or object in a sentence.  ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We use <b>possessive 's</b> to indicate possession. Place this particle at the end of the subject that possesses the noun you are talking about. </br></br> For example: </br>The <b>teacher's notes </b>about data warehouse are very useful. (The notes belong to the teacher. <i>Teacher</i> carries the <b>'s</b>)    </br> </br>  If the owner is singular, use the possessive 's at the end of the subject.<br/><br/>  Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">The <b>company's </b>data warehouse is really huge.</span><br/><br/>  If the owner is on its plural form use (') after the plural <strong>s </strong>of the subject. <br/><br/>  Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">You have to enter the <b>employees</b><b>' </b> transactions to the warehouse daily.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Our organization's data is stored in a data warehouse.   ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Managers' decisions are based on the information entered in the data warehouse.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "data warehouse ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a database designed for analysis ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well, I have to start working on the data warehouse, but I don't have any idea about that.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le02ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "manager ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person in charge of a business", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Managers' decisions are based on the information entered in the data warehouse.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le02ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "hidden ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "that is not visible", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The last one is data mining: it can discover knowledge by finding hidden patterns; this one can show findings in visual versions.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le02ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "second", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to support", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Another one is about analytical processing: it seconds analytical processing of information by analytical operations.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le02ob10aud04", "type": "au