"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n3le02ob10re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "<strong>Johanna</strong>: Hi, Samuel.<br/><strong>Samuel</strong>: Hi! Johanna. How can I help you?<br/><strong>Johanna</strong>: Well, I have to start working on the data warehouse, but I don't have any idea about that. <br/><strong>Samuel</strong>: I know everything related to the data warehouse, but I don't know if I'm able to explain it in an appropriate way. You know, I'm not good at it.<br/><strong>Johanna</strong>: Don't worry; I really appreciate your help.<br/><strong>Samue</strong>l: Ok, let me tell you what I know. A data warehouse is a database that companies implement  for analytical processes instead of real-time business operations. Modern organizations are able to organize their data in a data warehouse because it works with extent queries, and it helps us understand information at any time in a company. For example, our organization's data is stored in a data warehouse. <br/>", "image": "enpe7n3le02ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "53000", "text": "<strong>Johanna</strong>: Ok, what about its features?<br/><strong>Samuel</strong>: The data warehouse has some features you need to remember: it's subject-oriented, which means you can determine data by the subject; integrated, so the information appears in a uniform format;  time variant, which is why we are able to use information in specific periods of time; and non-volatile, since its information cannot change once it is entered. Managers' decisions are based on the information entered in the data warehouse. For example, modern organizations store a huge amount of data in the form of transactions that become database records for further analysis.<br/>", "image": "enpe7n3le02ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "99000", "text": "<strong>Johanna</strong>: Is there any other important information?<br/><strong>Samuel</strong>: Yes! You need to be able to work with the three different types of data warehouses that exist. One is related to information processing; it basically treats information by statistical analysis. I mean, it analyses charts or graphs. The other one is about analytical processing: it seconds the analytical processing of information by implementing analytical operations. The last one is data mining: it can discover information by finding hidden patterns.", "image": "enpe7n3le02ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n3le02ob10re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 4, "type": "audio"}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}